        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0ea982dc-2faf-5b0b-9696-15d58cf14008",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robbie Coltrane, J. K. Rowling, Tony Forsyth, Emile Charles, Bruce Payne\n- Characters: Rubeus Hagrid, Valentin Dmitrovich Zukovsky, Dr. Eddie \"Fitz\" Fitzgerald, Annabelle\n- Works: Harry Potter, GoldenEye, The World Is Not Enough, Cracker, The Fruit Machine, Wonderland\n\nFacts:\n- Robbie Coltrane was born Anthony Robert McMillan on 30 March 1950 and is a Scottish actor and author.\n- The Fruit Machine, released in 1988 and known in the United States as Wonderland, is a British film thriller starring Tony Forsyth, Emile Charles, Bruce Payne, and Robbie Coltrane.\n- Robbie Coltrane played the role of Annabelle in the 1988 film The Fruit Machine.\n- Robbie Coltrane played Dr. Eddie \"Fitz\" Fitzgerald in the British TV series Cracker during the 1990s.\n- Robbie Coltrane is known for playing Valentin Dmitrovich Zukovsky in the James Bond films GoldenEye and The World Is Not Enough.\n- Robbie Coltrane is known for playing Rubeus Hagrid in the Harry Potter films.\n- Rubeus Hagrid is a fictional character in the Harry Potter book series written by J. K. Rowling.\n- Robbie Coltrane was appointed OBE.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
